    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<p>AOHP evaluated its security model on a purpose-built annotated payment app covering five check categories: sensitive display, ordinary actions, sensitive actions, unsupported access, and sensitive events. All five passed — sensitive plaintext never reached the agent context, ordinary non-sensitive flows proceeded without unnecessary friction, and state-changing actions required explicit user consent.</p>
</section>

<!-- ─────────────── §05 ─────────────── -->
<section id="s-results" data-code="results">
<div class="section-no">05 — Results</div>
<h2>+21% Completion, −52% Tokens, Zero Leaks</h2>
<p>AOHP was evaluated using the OpenClaw agent on 30 real-world mobile tasks spanning six capability categories: GUI operation, non-GUI operation (file/shell work), event capture (transient notifications), multi-source information retrieval, memory management, and hybrid cross-capability workflows. The same agent ran on both stock Android and AOHP.</p>

